{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern","id":1144138,"title":"What does it take to create a Wyld Caern","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-26T11:35:23-07:00","id":1144138,"title":"What does it take to create a Wyld Caern","content":"I understand that only places that are purest wilderness can become a Caern dedicated to the Wyld, but what about places that Wyld spirits congregate? For instance, say you have a bunch of Haunters and they have used one specific spot for years as their training center on Earth for Pandemonium training. Sure, it's a deeply urban area, but it has been bathed in Wyld energy for a long time. Going by the rules it seems like this should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:46:30-07:00","id":1144146,"title":"","content":"Haunters aren't Wyld enough to qualify for Werewolf's purposes, nor are any places settled by humanity. One might spring up around a former city that was abandoned and reclaimed by encroachment of the wilderness, but that sort of thing is more of an &quot;after humanity&quot; scenario.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's doubtful that Garou or Fera could make them &quot;easily&quot; with the Rite of Caern Building, and if they have trouble with it, wraiths aren't going to manage it with just their normal, small-scale powers, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-26-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:15:28-07:00","id":1144160,"title":"","content":"Their back story states specifically that their power came about from a pact they made with the Wyld and every time they use Pandemonium they are channeling the Wyld itself. They can literally burn specters with Wyld fire, and warp the reality around them with Wyld powers that come across as scaled down versions of Break Reality. <br /> <br /> Though I can agree with the &quot;settled by humanity part.&quot; Still, I thought hundreds of Wraiths using Wyldfire and Tempus Fugit over a period of years might affect the area spiritually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-26-2017, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:30:50-07:00","id":1144167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1144160#post1144160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their back story states specifically that their power came about from a pact they made with the Wyld and every time they use Pandemonium they are channeling the Wyld itself. They can literally burn specters with Wyld fire, and warp the reality around them with Wyld powers that come across as scaled down versions of Break Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>All things that Wyldlings can do, but you don't see them generating Wyld caerns just by using their Charms a bunch of times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I can agree with the part about the &quot;settled by humanity part.&quot; Still, I thought hundreds of Wraiths using Wyldfire and Tempus Fugit over a period of years might affect the area spiritually. </div> </div> </div>The problem there is that the wraiths used to be human, which puts a bit of a limit on how much Wyld they're likely to be able to let in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:12:54-07:00","id":1144182,"title":"","content":"No, I don't mean that Wraiths can create Caerns, but I remember the Bone Gnawer book mentioning how the Gnawers will notice prospective Caerns that others would never consider, like a school house that absorbed a bunch of laughter over the years so it can now become a Caern dedicated to humor.<br /> <br /> Also, remember how significant the term &quot;used to be&quot; is. They are spirits whose spiritual bodies slowly warp, just like their minds and very essence as they channel the Wyld via the pact they made with it.<br /> <br /> Edit, I should add that I'm not simply talking about using their charms a bunch of times but rather the area would be like a giant nest of manifesting Haunters who tie themselves to the location, perhaps slowly turning it into an enormous haunt due to their powers being perpetually used on the other side of the Shroud. <br /> <br /> Still, I see your point that if a Garou who could persuade a hundred Wyldlings to stay in an area for years and manifest their powers through the Gauntlet continuously was enough to push an area to being right for a Wyld Caern, there would probably be at least a few more of those, so perhaps it really does depend on a wide range of factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-26-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T15:16:36-07:00","id":1144215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1144182#post1144182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't mean that Wraiths can create Caerns, but I remember the Bone Gnawer book mentioning how the Gnawers will notice prospective Caerns that others would never consider, like a school house that absorbed a bunch of laughter over the years so it can now become a Caern dedicated to humor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Garou who happen upon Wyld caerns are either Furies or Talons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, remember how significant the term &quot;used to be&quot; is. They are spirits whose spiritual bodies slowly warp, just like their minds and very essence as they channel the Wyld via the pact they made with it. </div> </div> </div>The Wyld doesn't honor or make pacts, though. It just is. Wraiths might have thought that they were making a pact, but they merely got changed by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit, I should add that I'm not simply talking about using their charms a bunch of times but rather the area would be like a giant nest of manifesting Haunters who tie themselves to the location, perhaps slowly turning it into an enormous haunt due to their powers being perpetually used on the other side of the Shroud. </div> </div> </div>That's a haunt, not a caern. A caern requires a specific rite to produce, along with a couple hundred points of Gnosis (you can make do with half, but the results won't be as impressive). And the rite is only performed at night, during the waxing of the moon, And if something of this magnitude were occurring, you can bet that specters would boil out of the Labyrinth en masse to stop it, much as how the rite typically turns into a siege as well as a race against time. Someone would notice and act, is what i'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I see your point that if a Garou who could persuade a hundred Wyldlings to stay in an area for years and manifest their powers through the Gauntlet continuously was enough to push an area to being right for a Wyld Caern, there would probably be at least a few more of those, so perhaps it really does depend on a wide range of factors. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That could reduce the difficulty of the rite, but it would not make it less demanding of the participants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T21:27:45-07:00","id":1144285,"title":"","content":"I never meant to imply that Wraiths could create a Caern, merely give a place the spiritual resonance it needs to be turned into a Caern. Cysts can grow anywhere, IIRC, so I thought there might be a chance.<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder what type of Caern you COULD build on this haunt. The only Caern type that I remember being built on graveyards or places that ghosts frequent are Caerns dedicated to Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-27-2017, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T22:30:32-07:00","id":1144289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1144285#post1144285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never meant to imply that Wraiths could create a Caern, merely give a place the spiritual resonance it needs to be turned into a Caern. Cysts can grow anywhere, IIRC, so I thought there might be a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it might very well cause Sour Ground, which is given as an example Wyld Threshold (a breakthrough of Wyld through the Gauntlet). Don't bury anyone in that graveyard...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I wonder what type of Caern you COULD build on this haunt. The only Caern type that I remember being built on graveyards or places that ghosts frequent are Caerns dedicated to Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>And that's what you'd likely get. Note that Thresholds in caerns are bad, bad news to Garou, and the Black Furies keep around a ritemistress who knows the Rite of Abcission to cut them out if they show up. The Wyld is not a helper when it comes to caerns, oddly enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T23:09:24-07:00","id":1144650,"title":"","content":"Wyld Caerns are tricky, I would say an important keyword to note is Virgin Territory, so they would very likely have to be someplace untouched by humanity. And if that wasn't the case they would need some crazy magic event to still be a wyld Caern, like say the site of a Meteor landing, or a place someone accidently caused time and space to blitz out wonkily enough to wipe out all but the most chaotic resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T23:12:35-07:00","id":1145449,"title":"","content":"The Wyld is chaotic, but also lively and creative. Destructive chaos might damage and weaken the Gauntlet, but I'd expect the presence of the dead to prevent a location from becoming fertile ground for a caern. I'd expect it to become a blighted, barren wilderness, more like the &quot;blasted heath&quot; in Lovecraft's short story, &quot;The Colour Out of Space,&quot; where freaky stuff can happen, but none of it is healthy. It might actually become the kind of place that attracts banes and other wyrm creatures, who'd like an opportunity to reach across a weakened spot in the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T23:24:23-07:00","id":1145452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1144285#post1144285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I wonder what type of Caern you COULD build on this haunt. The only Caern type that I remember being built on graveyards or places that ghosts frequent are Caerns dedicated to Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the pick on the Caern's type is on Gaia, but the ritemaster may attempt to ask for something specific. Creating a Caern of Healing on a graveyard should still not be possible, though, try to align the options with the place at your disposal.<br /> <br /> But remember that death -and specifically undeath- is Wyrm-aligned, not Wyld. A wraith-haunted location is probably going to be cleansed and exorcised before any Theurge will even attempt a rite of Caern building, unless we're talking about BSD shamans and Wyrm caerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T08:11:12-07:00","id":1145531,"title":"","content":"By definition, wraiths and Spectes alike are of the Wyrm. While yes, Haunters DO channel the Wyld, I view their Wyld-fueled Arcanos as a desperate act on the Wyld's part. So little of the Wyld exists in the Dark Umbra that the Wyld made its pact with the Haunter Guild's founders in a desperate attempt to simply survive amidst all that Oblivion!<br /> <br /> As to caerns: sure, why not? But they <i>wouldn't</i> be Wyld-caerns. They'd be VERY Wyrm-y!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T12:41:33-07:00","id":1145605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1145531#post1145531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition, wraiths and Spectes alike are of the Wyrm. While yes, Haunters DO channel the Wyld, I view their Wyld-fueled Arcanos as a desperate act on the Wyld's part. So little of the Wyld exists in the Dark Umbra that the Wyld made its pact with the Haunter Guild's founders in a desperate attempt to simply survive amidst all that Oblivion!<br /> <br /> As to caerns: sure, why not? But they <i>wouldn't</i> be Wyld-caerns. They'd be VERY Wyrm-y!</div> </div> </div> </div>Spectres yes, wraiths no, as they have to have a Shadow with permanent Angst higher than the wraith's Willpower to ping on Sense Wyrm. Also, Wraith's perspective on what goes on in the Middle Umbra and what lives there is going to be a bit off, and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T13:35:57-07:00","id":1145620,"title":"","content":"Well, in the Revised editions' metaplot, the Sixth Great Maelstrom heaved up momentarily into the Middle Umbra, and deposited wraiths and Spectres into certain Middle Umbral Realms, such as the Atrocity Realm and the Battlefield, so they might not be as ignorant as you'd think.<br /> <br /> However....<br /> <br /> ...that was Revised. Wr20 might retcon all of that, so, my example may no longer be canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T17:24:27-07:00","id":1145680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144138-what-does-it-take-to-create-a-wyld-caern?p=1145620#post1145620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in the Revised editions' metaplot, the Sixth Great Maelstrom heaved up momentarily into the Middle Umbra, and deposited wraiths and Spectres into certain Middle Umbral Realms, such as the Atrocity Realm and the Battlefield, so they might not be as ignorant as you'd think.<br /> <br /> However....<br /> <br /> ...that was Revised. Wr20 might retcon all of that, so, my example may no longer be canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wraiths mostly got heaved into the Atrocity Realm. That's a far cry from the standard MU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}